cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "drift-equilibrium: steady-state racing-car drift equilibrium, fold continuation, design optimization and LQR stabilization"
message: "If you use this code, please cite the repository (and the accompanying course report)."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ye
    given-names: Junhao
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-08
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yejunhao031018/drift-equilibrium"
keywords:
  - racing car
  - vehicle dynamics
  - drift equilibrium
  - nonlinear least squares
  - continuation
  - fold bifurcation
  - augmented Lagrangian
  - LQR
abstract: >-
  Solves the steady-state drifting equilibrium of a three-degree-of-freedom
  single-track vehicle with brush tires and a rear friction circle, maps the
  grip and drift branches with pseudo-arclength continuation, locates fold
  bifurcations with an extended system, optimizes vehicle parameters with an
  augmented Lagrangian on top of implicit-function reduction, and stabilizes
  the drift equilibrium with an LQR designed from the linearization.
